<Layout metadata={metadata}><article class="prose prose-lg mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-20"><p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary">Sourcing guide · Materials</p><h1>How to choose the right rosary bead material</h1><p class="lead">The right material depends on your target price, preferred weight, finish, and gifting occasion. Wood offers warmth, glass feels more formal, acrylic supports price-sensitive volume, and natural stone creates a premium impression.</p><h2>Quick comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Material</th><th>Best for</th><th>Buyer consideration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Wood</td><td>Natural, traditional collections</td><td>Grain and shade vary</td></tr><tr><td>Glass</td><td>Ceremonies and gifts</td><td>Heavier and more reflective</td></tr><tr><td>Acrylic</td><td>Volume programs</td><td>Broad color range</td></tr><tr><td>Natural stone</td><td>Premium gifting</td><td>Higher weight and cost</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Ask for samples before committing</h2><p>Photography cannot fully communicate weight, surface texture, translucency, or color variation. For larger programs, compare physical samples under the lighting used in your shop or product photography.</p><a class="btn-primary no-underline" href="/contact">Discuss your sourcing brief</a></article></Layout>

